=== layout: two-panels


@left

![Slide image 5](assets/lect05f-degrees_of_dominance/image_005.png)

@right

- Each gene is independent, [multiplication rule]{color=orange}
- Incompleteness does not matter, since we are discussing genotype.
- (b) MM is ¼, SS is ¼, and tt is ¼
- [¼ × ¼ × ¼ = 1/64]{color=orange}
- (c) MM [or]{color=blue} mm is ½, SS [or]{color=blue} ss is ½, TT [or]{color=blue} tt is ½
- [½ × ½ × ½ = 1/8]{color=orange}

=== layout: section

# Codominance

## The phenotype of the heterozygote displays both alleles independently, without blending,  allowing both traits to be seen separately.

=== layout: one-panel

# Codominance

@body

- The heterozygote&rsquo;s phenotype expresses both alleles independently and distinctly.
- Neither allele is masked; both traits appear side by side without blending.
- Example\: In certain species of chickens, the allele for black feathers (B) is codominant with the allele for white feathers (W), resulting in offspring with checkered or speckled feathers (BW).

