=== layout: one-panel


@body

- A child has a blood type B and the father has blood type A. What are the possible blood types for the mother?
- child\: [BO]{color=red} or BB
- father\: [AO]{color=red} or AA
- only possible scenario, is that the child received the O allele from the father.
- implies that the child is BO and the father is AO

- A. A
- B. B
- C. AB
- D. O

=== layout: one-panel


@body

- A child has a blood type B and the father has blood type A. What are the possible blood types for the mother?
- child\: [BO]{color=red} or BB
- father\: [AO]{color=red} or AA
- only possible scenario, is that the child received the O allele from the father.
- implies that the child is BO and the father is AO
- child has to receive the B allele from the mother.

- A. A
- B. B
- C. AB
- D. O

=== layout: one-panel

# Child type B; father type A

@body

- Possible genotypes: child [BO]{color=red} or BB; father [AO]{color=red} or AA
- Child receives O from father: child BO; father AO
- Mother supplies B: AB, BB, or BO
- Mother blood type: B or AB

- A. A
- B. B
- C. AB
- D. O

